# KiCad installs the contents of this file into the plugin's virtual
# environment, and marks the plugin "ready" only when `pip install -r` succeeds.
#
# dodplace deliberately installs nothing here:
#   * the plugin shim (main.py) uses the standard library only, so it runs on
#     whatever interpreter KiCad provides;
#   * the real dependencies (numpy, kicad-python, pdfplumber...) live in the
#     project's own uv environment, which the shim invokes.
#
# The file must exist even though it is empty of packages: without it KiCad
# fails the dependency job and never registers the action.
